    "q-129775": {
      "dom_id": "question-129775",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Let $a$ denote the approximation of $g(1)$ found in part 5. According to the alternating series error bound, we have that \n\n$$\n|g(1)-a|<k\n$$\n\n for some real number $k.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $k\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that $g(1)$ represents the sum of the convergent alternating series, while the approximation $a$ represents the fourth partial sum of this series:\n\n$$\ng(1)=S={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n},\\,a={s}_{4}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n|g(1)-a|=|S-{s}_{4}|.\n$$\n\nWe also know that ${a}_{5}=\\frac{1}{40}.$ Therefore, according to the alternating series error bound, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|S-{s}_{4}| & <|{a}_{5}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{1}{40}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{40}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
